# `server.js` — LawGPT OpenAI API Proxy

## Overview

This file creates a small **Express.js server** that acts as a proxy between the LawGPT browser application and the OpenAI API.

The basic request flow is:

```text
LawGPT Browser
     │
     │ POST /api/chat
     ▼
Express Server (localhost:3000)
     │
     │ POST /v1/responses
     ▼
OpenAI API
     │
     ▼
Express Server
     │
     │ JSON response
     ▼
LawGPT Browser
```

The main purpose of this server is to keep the OpenAI API key on the server side. The LawGPT frontend does not communicate directly with OpenAI. Instead, it sends requests to this local server, which adds the API key and forwards the request to OpenAI.

