# 6. Restricting API-key changes to localhost

**Lines 37–46:**

```js
function requireLocalhost(req, res, next) {
  const ip = req.ip || req.connection.remoteAddress || "";
  const isLocal = ip === "127.0.0.1" || ip === "::1" || ip === "::ffff:127.0.0.1";
  if (!isLocal) {
    return res.status(403).json({ error: { message: "Settings changes are only allowed from localhost." } });
  }
  next();
}
```

`requireLocalhost()` is Express middleware that checks the IP address of the incoming request.

It allows requests from localhost:

```text
127.0.0.1
::1
::ffff:127.0.0.1
```

These are IPv4/IPv6 representations of the local machine.

If the request does not originate from localhost, the function returns:

```text
HTTP 403 Forbidden
```

with the message:

```text
Settings changes are only allowed from localhost.
```

This is important because the API-key endpoint allows a client to modify the stored OpenAI API key.

