# 7. Updating `.env_me`

**Lines 49–66:**

```js
function upsertEnvKey(key) {
  let lines = [];
  if (fs.existsSync(ENV_PATH)) {
    lines = fs.readFileSync(ENV_PATH, "utf8").split("\n");
  }
  let found = false;
  lines = lines.map(line => {
    if (line.startsWith("OPENAI_API_KEY=")) {
      found = true;
      return `OPENAI_API_KEY=${key}`;
    }
    return line;
  });
  if (!found) lines.push(`OPENAI_API_KEY=${key}`);
  // Drop stray trailing blank lines, then write back with one trailing newline.
  while (lines.length && lines[lines.length - 1] === "") lines.pop();
  fs.writeFileSync(ENV_PATH, lines.join("\n") + "\n", { mode: 0o600 });
}
```

The `upsertEnvKey()` function updates the API key stored in `.env_me`.

The term **upsert** means:

> Update the existing value if it exists; otherwise insert a new value.

### Reading the existing file

```js
if (fs.existsSync(ENV_PATH)) {
  lines = fs.readFileSync(ENV_PATH, "utf8").split("\n");
}
```

If `.env_me` already exists, the function reads it and splits it into individual lines.

This means the function can modify the API key without overwriting unrelated settings.

For example, if `.env_me` contains:

```text
PORT=3000
OPENAI_API_KEY=old-key
```

the `PORT=3000` line is preserved.

### Finding the existing API key

```js
if (line.startsWith("OPENAI_API_KEY=")) {
```

The function searches for the line containing the existing API key.

If it finds one, it replaces that line:

```js
return `OPENAI_API_KEY=${key}`;
```

### Adding the key if it does not exist

```js
if (!found) lines.push(`OPENAI_API_KEY=${key}`);
```

If there was no existing `OPENAI_API_KEY` entry, a new one is appended.

### Writing the file

```js
fs.writeFileSync(ENV_PATH, lines.join("\n") + "\n", { mode: 0o600 });
```

Writes the updated contents back to `.env_me`.

The `0o600` permission setting is intended to restrict the file so that only its owner can read or write it on systems that support Unix file permissions.

