# 8. Checking whether an API key is configured

**Lines 69–74:**

```js
app.get("/api/key-status", (req, res) => {
  res.json({
    configured: Boolean(apiKey),
    last4: apiKey ? apiKey.slice(-4) : null
  });
});
```

This creates the endpoint:

```text
GET /api/key-status
```

LawGPT can call this endpoint to determine whether an API key has been configured.

The server returns information such as:

```json
{
  "configured": true,
  "last4": "1234"
}
```

The complete API key is never returned.

Instead:

```js
apiKey.slice(-4)
```

extracts only the last four characters.

This allows the LawGPT Settings panel to display that a key has been configured without exposing the entire key to the browser.

