## 10.1 Checking for an API key

```js
if (!apiKey) {
  return res.status(400).json({
    error: {
      message: "No API key configured yet..."
    }
  });
}
```

Before contacting OpenAI, the server checks whether an API key exists.

If there is no key, the request stops and LawGPT receives an HTTP `400` error.

---

## 10.2 Getting the model and input

```js
const { model, input } = req.body || {};
```

LawGPT is expected to send a request containing at least:

```json
{
  "model": "...",
  "input": "..."
}
```

The server extracts those two values from `req.body`.

It then verifies that both are present:

```js
if (!model || !input)
```

If either is missing, the server returns a `400` error.

